{
  "id": 463542418,
  "iid": 23880,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Fix invisible separator spacing in filter expression toolbar",
  "description": "Disabled QFrame separators are added between display filter buttons to\nprovide a thin visual divider. However, separators were created for\nevery dfilter_buttons UAT entry, including entries that resolve to\nsubmenu items (labels containing PARENT_SEPARATOR). Since submenu\nitems are added to a QMenu and not to the toolbar itself, their\ncorresponding QFrame widgets are invisible but still occupy ~1 px of\ntoolbar space each. With many submenu entries this causes progressively\nwider gaps between the visible toolbar buttons.\n\nMove the separator creation into the else branch that handles\ntoolbar-level actions so that separators are only added between buttons\nthat are actually placed on the toolbar.\n\nFixes: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/21087",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T11:04:18.860Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-17T06:54:41.278Z",
